1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:00,626
Hello!

2
00:00:00,626 --> 00:00:04,199
Today we'll learn 'double vowels' and 'semivowel glides',

3
00:00:04,199 --> 00:00:07,020
where two sounds slide together. Let's begin!

4
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:12,239
When two vowels join and sound like one,

5
00:00:12,239 --> 00:00:13,771
we call it a 'double vowel'.

6
00:00:13,771 --> 00:00:16,890
Its key feature is that your mouth shape glides smoothly.

7
00:00:21,070 --> 00:00:26,075
Hidden at the front of a double vowel is a quick 'semivowel'.

8
00:00:26,075 --> 00:00:29,193
There are two kinds: a glide from 'ㅣ',

9
00:00:29,193 --> 00:00:31,490
and a glide from 'ㅗ' or 'ㅜ'.

10
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,313
First, the 'ㅣ' glide.

11
00:00:36,313 --> 00:00:45,100
Slide quickly from 'ㅣ' to 'ㅏ' and you get 'ㅑ' — the sound in 야 (ya).

12
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:55,635
The same way, 'ㅓ' becomes 'ㅕ', 'ㅗ' becomes 'ㅛ',

13
00:00:55,635 --> 00:01:02,240
and 'ㅜ' becomes 'ㅠ', all gliding gently from 'ㅣ'.

14
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:14,876
Practice with words: 'ㅑ' in 야구 (baseball),

15
00:01:14,876 --> 00:01:20,739
'ㅕ' in 여우 (fox), 'ㅛ' in 요리 (cooking),

16
00:01:20,739 --> 00:01:26,920
'ㅠ' in 우유 (milk). Let your mouth glide.

17
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:36,490
'ㅐ' also glides to 'ㅒ', and 'ㅔ' to 'ㅖ',

18
00:01:36,490 --> 00:01:43,880
as in 얘기 (talk, ㅒ) and 예의 (manners, ㅖ).

19
00:01:47,370 --> 00:01:50,848
Now the 'ㅗ', 'ㅜ' glide.

20
00:01:50,848 --> 00:02:00,830
Slide from 'ㅗ' to 'ㅏ' and you get 'ㅘ' — the 과 sound in 사과 (apple).

21
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:12,753
'ㅜ' plus 'ㅓ' makes 'ㅝ', 'ㅗ' plus 'ㅣ' makes 'ㅚ',

22
00:02:12,753 --> 00:02:17,047
and 'ㅜ' plus 'ㅣ' makes 'ㅟ'.

23
00:02:17,047 --> 00:02:21,340
Round your lips, then open.

24
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:35,969
Practice: 'ㅘ' in 사과 (apple), 'ㅝ' in 샤워 (shower),

25
00:02:35,969 --> 00:02:42,606
'ㅚ' in 외투 (coat), 'ㅟ' in 가위 (scissors).

26
00:02:42,606 --> 00:02:46,180
Feel the round glide.

27
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:54,794
Last is 'ㅢ', a special glide from 'ㅡ' to 'ㅣ'.

28
00:02:54,794 --> 00:02:59,990
Pronounce it like the 의 in 의자 (chair).

29
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:09,894
In sum, 'ㅑ', 'ㅕ', 'ㅛ', 'ㅠ', 'ㅘ', 'ㅝ', 'ㅟ', 'ㅚ',

30
00:03:09,894 --> 00:03:15,838
'ㅢ' are all double vowels made by a gliding semivowel.

31
00:03:15,838 --> 00:03:19,360
Remember the flow of your mouth.

32
00:03:22,170 --> 00:03:25,295
Today we learned double vowels and semivowel glides.

33
00:03:25,295 --> 00:03:27,878
Look for double vowels in words around you.

34
00:03:27,878 --> 00:03:28,960
See you next time!

